# MLISP.

**Authors:** Smith, David Canfield

## Abstract
MLISP (meta-LISP) is a high level list-processing and symbol-manipulation language based on the programing language LISP (List Processor). MLISP programs are translated into LISP programs and then executed or compiled. MLISP exists for two purposes: (1) to facilitate the writing and understanding of LISP programs; (2) to remedy certain important deficiencies in the list-processing ability of LISP. (Author/MF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED047526

